# ╔═╡ 75e3fe79-feae-4800-9445-0f5e3cf97a0e
md"
---
##### 0. Introduction
First, we derive all *first-order* antiderivatives of the *Scotch-Yoke-Oscillator(SYO)* in *parallel*. A first-order antiderivative in the context of *SYO* is based on the theoretical correct *state* function $f_x(τ) = x(τ) = cos(τ)$, $f_v(τ) = v(τ) = sin(τ)$, $f_a(τ) = a(τ) = -cos(τ)$, $f_j(τ) = j(τ) = -sin(τ)$. 

Then, starting with $f_j(τ) = j(τ)$ we compute all *higher-order* (=[*iterated*, *repeated*](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iterated_integral)) antiderivatives $F_a(j(τ)), F_v(F_a(f_j(τ))), F_x(F_v(F_a(f_j(τ))))$. 
Both approaches are computed by our *own* code and by reused code of package [*QuadGK.jl*](https://juliapackages.com/p/quadgk).
"

