###### 3.2 Numerical *Parallelized* AntiDerivatives
Each one of the antiderivatives $F_a(τ)=accelerationFromJerk(τ)$, $F_v(τ)=velocityFromAcceleration(τ)$, and $F_x(τ)=positionFromVelocity(τ)$ is computed from its *theoretical* correct derivative $f_j(τ)=jerk(τ), f_a(τ)=acc(τ), f_v(τ)=vel(τ)$. We call this approach *parallel*.

"

# ╔═╡ 80d36f05-8dd4-4c5b-b54e-d695b709532b
md"
---
###### 3.2.1 Numerical Antiderivatives
###### 1st *Method* of Function *Antiderivative* $F(x)$ with Continuous *Function Parameter* $f$

$F(x) = F(a) + \int_a^x f(x') dx' \approx c + \Delta x \sum_{i=1}^x f(x_i)\;;\; x_i \le x$

where:

$c = F(a),$

$\Delta x = \frac{|a-b|}{n}\;;\;\text{ where } n = \text{ number of intervals}$

$a + \frac{\Delta x}{2} \le x_i \le b - \frac{\Delta x}{2},$ 

$x_{i+1} = x_i + \Delta x.$

"

# ╔═╡ db44b28c-9d51-49d3-a7a3-3f665e98fcb9
function antiDerivative(   # --------------------------------- 1st method
#   +--------------------------------------------------------- functional argument f
#   |            +-------------------------------------------- number of intervals
#   |            |         +---------------------------------- lower limit a
#   |            |         |           +---------------------- upper limit x
#	|            |         |           |           +---------- integration constant c
#   |            |         |           |           |
#   v            v         v           v           v                        
	f::Function, n::Int64, a::Float64, x::Float64; c::Float64=0.0)::Tuple{Float64, Float64, Float64}
	myIntegral(f, n, a, x, c = c)   
end # function antiDerivative   

# ╔═╡ d0df5abd-47bb-4d84-ab99-18061471c981
md"
---
###### 2nd Method of Function Antiderivative $F(x)$ with *Vector* $fs$ of Discretized *Function* Values 

There is a *constraint* between upper integration limit $x = b - a$, $length([...,f_x[i],...]\ and\ \Delta x$:

$x = length([...,f_x[i],...]) \cdot \Delta x = n \Delta x$

and mappings

$(x, \frac{1}{\Delta x}) \mapsto n \left(= length([...,f_xx[i],...])\right)$

$(x, n) \mapsto \frac{x}{n} = \Delta x.$

So the second *method* of function $antiDerivative$ has *three* values:
- the *first* value is the *approximation* of *antiderivative* $F(x)$
- the *second* value is the *step width* $Δx$
- the *third* value is the reconstructed *interval length* $|a-b|$

$F(x)\approx c + \Delta x ∑_{i=1}^n [...,f_x[i],...]$

where: 

$f_x[i] = f(x_i),$

$a + \frac{\Delta x}{2} \le x_i \le b - \frac{\Delta x}{2},$ 

$x_{i+1} = x_i + \Delta x$

- the *third* value is the *reconstruction* of the integration bound $x$ dependent on the *length* $n$ of the *vector* of function values $length([...,f_xx[i],...])$ and step length $\Delta x$ 

$length([...,f_x[i],...]) \cdot \Delta x = n\Delta x \mapsto x$

The *approximation* of the antiderivative is:

$F(x) = F(a) + \int_a^x f(x') dx' \approx c + \Delta x \sum_{i=1}^n [...,f_x[i],...].$
"

# ╔═╡ f0ef09b2-285c-4d79-af72-66b239e237b6
function antiDerivative(   # ----------------------------- 2nd method
#   +----------------------------------------------------- vector of function values
#   |                    +-------------------------------- #intervals
#   |                    |         +---------------------- lower limit
#   |                    |         |           +---------- upper limit
#   |                    |         |           |
#   v                    v         v           v  
	fs::Vector{Float64}, n::Int64, a::Float64, x::Float64; c::Float64=0.0)::Tuple{Float64, Float64, Float64} 
	myIntegral(fs, n, a, x, c = c)
end # unction antiDerivative

# ╔═╡ a29a57ad-58ce-4843-8708-1a543c2f73ba
md"
---
###### 3rd Method of Function Antiderivative
"

# ╔═╡ e8f49745-f685-4b77-bc5f-26c9accf812b
function antiDerivative(   # ----------------------------- 3rd method
#   +----------------------------------------------------- vector of function values
#   |                    +-------------------------------- step width
#   |                    |              +----------------- index of upper limit
#   |                    |              |           
#   v                    v              v           
	fs::Vector{Float64}, Δx::Float64, ntemp::Int64; c::Float64=0.0)::Tuple{Float64, Float64, Float64} 
	myIntegral(fs, Δx, ntemp, c = c)
end # function antiDerivative

# ╔═╡ ff5cafdd-63f7-4b38-9a79-c9364b31fafc
